# L-SEA Space Apps - Git attribute rules
#
# Committed terrain grids are binary payloads used by the static build.
# Marking them binary keeps diffs/merges from treating them as text and
# prevents line-ending conversion from corrupting int16 arrays.
*.bin binary
*.jp2 binary

# Text files follow the repository convention: UTF-8 with LF line endings.
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.vue text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
